<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 6.0 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 6.0 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 6.0 percent in the week to May 28 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 5.6 percent.(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			     Latest week  Previous week  Year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  21.78	  21.46	     20.54</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	2.10	   2.31		1.90</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
